{"sequence":44,"timestamp":"2026-05-02T02:33:59.450689931Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-5594977e","body":"`combine_vss_wallets` can accept and authenticate recovered metadata from fewer than the threshold number of complete VSS shares. At `frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs:1205` it builds `verified_inputs` as the intersection of shares whose low and high halves both verify for the winning 24-word candidate, but `frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs:1211` only requires that intersection to be non-empty before deriving metadata. For a 3-of-5 24-word wallet, low-half recovery can succeed from shares {1,2,3} while high-half recovery succeeds from {3,4,5}, leaving only share 3 as a complete verified input. Then `derive_metadata` computes `is_duress` from that one input at `frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs:1378`/`frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs:1385`; a single tampered complete share with `is_duress=true` becomes a strict majority, `authenticate` can still pass because it validates xpub/network via no-passphrase rebuild, and `VssRecovery::rebuild_singlesig` permits passphrase use when `metadata.is_duress` is true at `frozenkrill-core/src/secret_sharing.rs:83`. Require at least the candidate threshold worth of distinct complete verified share identifiers before accepting a candidate and deriving metadata, or otherwise keep metadata unauthenticated so the candidate is rejected.","classification":"fix_current_bead","dedup_key":"aa3b78a4702d1ed7010a0b6dcf9c20743ce78488b29a9843413ad6cf4b2efdd1","reviewer_sources":[{"backend_family":"codex","model_id":"gpt-5.5-xhigh","reviewer_id":"reviewer-1"}],"run_id":"run-20260502013456","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
