{"sequence":66,"timestamp":"2026-05-02T02:56:01.628597865Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-3-5382e896","body":"Remove the `result` symlink committed at the repo root and add it to `.gitignore`.\n\nThe `result` symlink (currently pointing at `/nix/store/jh0d0mapva43v7g66jby7hmrxap57mck-frozenkrill-0.0.0`) was inadvertently staged by a ralph-burning checkpoint at commit `90e9c7e` when this run invoked `nix build`. `result` is a build-output symlink that nix recreates with a different store-hash on every code change, so committing it means future `nix build` invocations will show it as a stale-but-tracked file — every contributor will see it as a phantom diff in `git status` and risk re-committing the new path each time.\n\nFix steps in this bead:\n1. `rm result`\n2. add a `result` (or `result*` to also catch `result-1`, `result-bin`, …) entry to `.gitignore` next to the existing `target/` rule\n3. `git add .gitignore && git rm result`\n\nThis is in scope for the current bead because the artifact was created by *this* run's nix-build invocations and would otherwise leak into the bead's PR.","classification":"fix_current_bead","dedup_key":"a087bd5adcfeab80161890655d1fa1393cfd4f753a1ff6fb611df225039a2704","reviewer_sources":[{"backend_family":"claude","model_id":"claude-opus-4-7-max","reviewer_id":"reviewer-2"}],"run_id":"run-20260502013456","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
